# Define the script title
title = "Portrait Short"

# Define the genre of the film
genre = "Short"

# Define the film's director
director = "Your Name"

# Define the film's script
script = """
INT. FILM SET - DAY

The camera pans across the cityscape, showing the beauty of the world.

CUT TO:

A close-up shot of the main character, looking out at the view.

FADE TO BLACK.

CUT TO:

A montage of the main character's daily life, set to music.

FADE TO BLACK.

CUT TO:

The main character standing in front of a cityscape, looking out at the view.

FADE TO BLACK.

THE END.
"""

# Print the script
print("Script for", title)
print("Genre:", genre)
print("Directed by:", director)
print(script)
```

This script is for a portrait short film, where we follow the main character's daily life and showcase the beauty of the world around them. The film is a short and poignant look at the human experience
